From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gezim <gezimos@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Kompakt: the kompakt_aux service MuditaOS apps ask for

MuditaOS 2.0's apps (Weather, Phone, SMS, Recorder, InkApps and more) ask
Android for a system service named kompakt_aux and call isHwksOn() on it,
the Offline+ switch. KompaktOS has no such service, getSystemService
returns null and the apps die with a NullPointerException: Weather on
every network request, Recorder at start, Phone at the call button.

This adds the service with MuditaOS 2.0's interface, method for method and
in the same order, so the transaction codes match. It answers: the switch
from irqkey_state, the battery counters from /sys/kernel/battery_monitor,
the region from the modem version, location and crash reporting from
settings. It does not switch radios; the Kompakt app does that. Settings
that change the phone are ignored, with a log line, for callers that are
not the system and do not hold WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS, so a user app gets
no error and no effect.
